# FDD 28 review — "28 - Professional Learning - Processing" (Features 28.1-28.5).
# Ingested per abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/CONVENTIONS.md against the mied-v3 Professional
# Learning graph (proflearning-domain.ttl / proflearning-permissions.ttl /
# proflearning-api.ttl / proflearning-sequences.ttl, all loaded together), plus
# documents-api.ttl and communications-api.ttl/-capability.ttl for cross-domain
# satisfaction checks (document viewing, email/comment infrastructure).
#
# Source: "28 - Professional Learning - Processing.docx" (subtitle "28.1-28.5"). Read the
# .md sibling first, then unzipped the .docx for comments.xml/commentsExtended.xml and
# word/media (28 images, image1.png-image28.jpg). A second file in the same folder,
# "TBDeleted_ 28 - Professional Learning - Admin Processing.docx", is an earlier, less
# detailed draft of the same subject matter (its own filename says it's slated for
# deletion) — its .md was read and confirmed to be wholly superseded by the main
# document (same Business Specifications restated at lower fidelity, no numbered
# Addendum stories of its own, no wireframes); not separately ingested, consistent with
# CONVENTIONS.md's treatment of duplicate/superseded source material. One thing from it
# worth preserving: its own Dependencies section explicitly ties FDD 28 to "Public
# Search - Professional Learning Resources (31.5)" for catalog maintenance, corroborated
# below by a comments.xml thread (comment 17).
#
# Structure of the document and what's used as the Requirement unit:
# - A "Business Specifications" prose section + a "HIGH LEVEL SCENARIOS" paraphrase
#   table (43 rows) both restate the same admin-worklist/search/review actions at
#   coarser grain — the HLS table is skipped per CONVENTIONS.md (duplicative).
# - An "Addendum" with real Feature/story numbering (28.1.1-28.1.5, 28.3.1,
#   28.4.1-28.4.6, 28.5.3-28.5.8) is the primary Requirement unit used below. Feature
#   28.2 ("Publishing the Professional Learning Catalog") has no numbered stories at
#   all — the Addendum states outright that the feature "is no longer considered
#   necessary" because its own dependency (FDD 26's Feature 26.4, Professional Learning
#   Catalog) was itself dropped. Modeled as a single rejected Requirement (Req_28_2)
#   rather than forced into a numbered-story shape it doesn't have.
# - The Addendum's own numbering has two of the same quirks the FDD 29 pass already
#   found and named: (a) Feature 28.4 has a genuine duplicate-number collision — a
#   heading "28.4.3 As a... I need the system to store audit details when I edit..." is
#   immediately followed by a SECOND, unrelated story also numbered "28.4.3" ("I need to
#   review the Audit Log of a Program..."). Modeled as Req_28_4_3 and Req_28_4_3b, the
#   FDD's own literal numbers preserved, collision and all — same treatment FDD 29 used
#   for its own 29.4.3/29.4.4 collision. (b) Feature 28.5's numbering starts at 28.5.3,
#   not 28.5.1 — 28.5.1/28.5.2 are never defined anywhere in the document. The Business
#   Specifications prose's own Sponsor-worklist search/filter/results description (which
#   would be the natural 28.5.1/28.5.2 content, by analogy with 28.5.3/28.5.4's Program-
#   worklist search/filter) was apparently never promoted into the Addendum's own
#   numbering at all — the same "described and wireframed in Business Specs, never
#   promoted to a real Addendum number" pattern the FDD 29 pass found for three of its
#   own Business-Specification-only features. Modeled below with a synthetic
#   plrn:Req_28_BizSpec_SponsorWorklistSearch ID rather than silently absorbed into
#   28.5's numbering or silently dropped.
# - Several other real, wireframed Business-Specification-only capabilities are likewise
#   never given an Addendum number at all: Sponsor List view/edit/delete (Wireframes
#   7-8), the approved-Programs list and program withdraw (Wireframe 9), evaluation-
#   question-template maintenance, and Program Category/Program Description admin
#   maintenance. All modeled with synthetic plrn:Req_28_BizSpec_* IDs below, per the same
#   FDD-29-pattern reasoning as above — see the "Business-Specification-only
#   capabilities" section.
#
# Comments (11 total, via comments.xml): the most load-bearing thread is a genuine
# admin-editability CONTRADICTION resolved mid-review: comment 3 (Ross, 2025-12-05)
# states edit access to a Sponsor application is deliberately restricted to an Action +
# comments, NOT the application fields themselves; comment 4 (Ross, same day, later)
# notes this was "later discussed as potentially allowing a Sponsor Application to be
# editable... Need confirmation"; comment 5 (Dontje, 2026-01-28, ~2 months later)
# resolves it: "Yes, the Sponsor Application should be editable by the admin." The
# visible Addendum text (28.1.3, "The system provides an option to Edit the selected
# Sponsor application, allowing the administrator to modify any submitted field") already
# reflects the FINAL, resolved position — not the earlier-restricted one comment 3
# describes — so no correction to the modeled text was needed, but the contradiction
# itself (and how close the document came to shipping the earlier, narrower reading) is
# worth recording; see Question_SponsorApplicationEditabilityWasContested below. Comment
# 8/6/7 make the parallel point for Program applications (admin can edit ALL sections,
# no restriction ever proposed there) — consistent with 28.4.1's visible text, no
# correction needed. Comment 9 (Ross) is a naming-standardization note ("Audit Log" is
# the term of record, not "Activity Log" — the Business Specifications prose's own
# Wireframe 6 caption still says "Activity log", a stale term the Addendum's 28.4.3b/
# 28.5.7 correctly updated to "Audit Log"; not itself worth a separate Annotation).
# Comment 18 (Groom, 2026-02-02) on the evaluations-review passage says "Admin ability to
# manage/maintain the evaluations should be included in 14, this may belong with that
# admin functionality. Need to discuss" — an explicit, UNRESOLVED cross-FDD scope
# question about whether 28.4.6 belongs here or in FDD 14 (Professional Learning Admin);
# modeled as Question_EvaluationReviewFddOwnershipUnresolved. Comment 17 (Groom,
# 2026-01-30) ties catalog/search maintenance to FDD 31.5 and flags that admin-side
# search-function maintenance has no described mechanism yet — folded into the
# BizSpec catalog-maintenance coverage-gap notes below. Comments 10, 12, 16 are minor
# single-word/single-line notes ("Approved Sponsors", "no longer relevant" re: an
# internal review artifact, "Can this assumption be confirmed?") with no independently
# resolvable finding and are not modeled as separate Annotations.
#
# Tracked changes: not inspected in detail for this pass (a lower-volume document than
# FDD 11/16 or 29; no comment thread pointed at a stale-vs-corrected-text situation that
# would require it).
#
# Wireframes: 14 are captioned "Wireframe N" in the Business Specifications prose
# (1-14); the .docx's word/media folder holds 28 image files total, not 14 — document
# order (confirmed via document.xml's r:embed sequence, which runs image1 through
# image28 essentially in file-number order) shows roughly twice as many embeds as
# captions, because several images are decorative/repeated chrome (a State-of-Michigan
# seal, repeated header icons) rather than distinct wireframes, and a cluster of later
# images (~ image20-28) are higher-fidelity Sponsor/Coordinator-facing screens (program
# creation, attendance submission with an attestation checkbox, an Attendance/
# Evaluations tab view) that read as reference material carried over from the
# Sponsor-side FDD (26/27) rather than this FDD's own Professional-Learning-Admin-facing
# deliverable — this FDD's own actors are exclusively "Professional Learning
# Administrator" throughout the Business Specifications and Addendum text. Four images
# were viewed and extracted: image1.png (Wireframe 1: Sponsor worklist search/results —
# confirmed; ALSO reveals a persistent admin tab bar "Sponsor Worklist | Program
# Worklist | Sponsor List | Program List | Category/Program description | Coupons and
# Payments | Email Sponsors" not fully described anywhere in the prose text — see
# Question_CouponsAndPaymentsTabUndocumented below), image2.png (Wireframe 2: Review
# Sponsor Application — confirms the Action/Comment/Comment-History layout matching
# 28.1.3/28.1.5), image9.png (Wireframe 7: Sponsor List search/results — confirms
# Sponsor-name/Sponsor-ID/Include-Inactive filters and the Active-column checkbox
# layout), and image28.jpg (an uncaptioned, higher-fidelity Attendance/Evaluations tab
# view for a Coordinator-facing "{Program_Name}" screen, extracted as
# addendum-a-attendance-evaluation-tabs.jpg — background context for 28.4.5/28.4.6, not
# confidently mapped to any one of the 14 captioned wireframes or to this FDD's own
# PL-Admin actor scope). The remaining ~24 images were sampled by position (early/mid/
# late in the document) rather than individually described — per CONVENTIONS.md's depth-
# calibration guidance — and confirmed to be consistent with the two clusters described
# above (PL-Admin worklist/list screens matching the numbered stories; Sponsor/
# Coordinator-side reference screens outside this FDD's own actor scope), not a distinct
# undocumented feature area.

@prefix sd:    <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:> .
@prefix oa:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix plrn:  <urn:solutiondesign:instance:proflearning:> .
@prefix docs:  <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:> .
@prefix comm:  <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:> .

#################################################################
# Source documents
#################################################################

plrn:Fdd28Doc a sd:SourceDocument ;
    sd:docType "fdd" ;
    sd:section "functional-design-docs/28 - Professional Learning - Processing/28 - Professional Learning - Processing.docx" ;
    sd:notes "Covers Features 28.1-28.5 (document's own subtitle: '28 - Professional Learning - Processing (28.1 - 28.5)'). Authors Vidhya Punniyamoorthy / Beth Dontje (DTMB); approved by Beth Dontje (MDE) and Caitlin Groom (CEPI), both 08/05/2025 per the signoff table — but comments.xml contains dated entries through 2026-02-02, well after that signoff date (same post-signoff-revision pattern the FDD 29 review already found in its own sibling document), meaning the document continued to be actively revised/reviewed after its nominal approval date. A companion document in the same folder, 'TBDeleted_ 28 - Professional Learning - Admin Processing.docx', is an earlier, superseded draft of the same subject matter — read and confirmed wholly superseded (see this file's header note), not separately modeled." .

